{%- comment -%}
  The 35mm conversion strip, as its own section so its photos and copy can be managed on their
  own in the theme editor.

  Photos come from 'Sample scan' blocks. The frame COUNT is fixed by how much film the driver
  needs to cover the widest viewport without running out of stock, so it cannot follow the block
  count: the blocks are a pool tiled across the strip. With none, it falls back to the bundled
  ts-strip-*.jpg assets.

  Its CSS and JS are still part of the page-wide bundle rendered by tonescan-hero, not a slice of
  their own. Splitting those out is the job for when the contact sheet reuses this.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tonescan-landing tw:text-neutral-200">
  {%- comment -%} The lite template (page.tonescan-lite) is a trimmed variant for early testers.
     Detected from the template suffix, so markup is shared rather than duplicated. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ts_minimal = false -%}
  {%- if template.suffix == 'tonescan-lite' -%}{%- assign ts_minimal = true -%}{%- endif -%}


  {%- comment -%} ==================== 4 · CONVERSION STRIP ====================
       A strip of frames stepping leftward. Everything right of the middle is still a negative,
       everything past it has been converted. The frame that lands in the middle flips through
       a white flash, then the strip steps on. Motion is deliberately not continuous: step,
       settle, convert, settle. Placeholder pairs for now, cycling four real frames.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ts-conv-sec tw:relative tw:overflow-hidden tw:border-y tw:border-white/10 tw:bg-white/[0.015]">
    <div class="ts-conv-head tw:relative tw:z-[1] tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:px-[15px] tw:pt-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:pt-[120px] tw:text-left">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-[#111114] tw:md:text-[46px]">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
      <p class="tw:mt-[18px] tw:text-[17px] tw:leading-[1.6] tw:text-[#55565c]">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Forced off on lite as well as by the toggle: the gallery it points at is
         not on that template, and an anchor with no target scrolls nowhere. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_scans_cta and ts_minimal == false and section.settings.cta_text != blank -%}
      <a class="ts-conv-cta" href="{{ section.settings.cta_link | default: '#gallery' }}">{{ section.settings.cta_text }} <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span></a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Shooting notes. Lives in the head so it falls under the CTA on phones, and
         gets lifted into the empty dark column on desktop. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
      <div class="ts-conv-note">{{ section.settings.note }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Two identical strips stacked and driven by one transform. Their masks are
       complements, so the negative owns the right, the positive owns the left, and they cross
       through each other in the middle. A frame converts by travelling, not by flipping.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} Two identical strips stacked and driven by one transform. Their masks are
       complements, so the negative owns the right, the positive owns the left, and the hard
       edge between them sits in the gap after the centred frame. Both layers MUST hold the
       same number of frames or they drift apart. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} Backdrop the film sits over. Reuses the hero's particle layers so the two
       sections share a texture. The negative half of the strip is translucent, so this is what
       shows through the orange base, blurred. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ts-conv-bg" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="ts-hero-particles"><span class="p1"></span><span class="p2"></span><span class="p3"></span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="ts-conv" role="img" aria-label="A strip of film frames converting from negative to positive as they travel">
      {%- comment -%} Both layers must get identical edge printing: they are stacked and crossfaded,
         so any difference between them would show as the text changing at the changeover. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'tonescan-strip-layer', kind: 'pos', pool: section.blocks, stock: section.settings.edge_stock, batch: section.settings.edge_batch %}
      {% render 'tonescan-strip-layer', kind: 'neg', pool: section.blocks, stock: section.settings.edge_stock, batch: section.settings.edge_batch %}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Bloom over the film, not behind it: a glow that stops at the strip edge does
       not read as light coming off the stock. Sits above the strip and washes both it and the
       background around it. {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="ts-conv-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    {%- comment -%} Hover affordance for the drag. Nothing on a piece of film says "grab me", and
       a written label would look wrong printed across it, so the cursor becomes a dot instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="ts-conv-dot" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
  </section>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "toneScan conversion strip",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "name": "Sample scan",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Photo"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Any shape works, the frame crops to fit. Add one block per photo; they are tiled across the strip in order, so around 12 or more avoids a visible repeat. With no blocks the built-in set is used."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Copy"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "Negatives in, photographs out."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subtitle",
      "default": "One pass over the roll, no per-frame corrections. You check a roll now instead of rescuing it."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "note",
      "label": "Right column text",
      "default": "<p>All frames here were converted on automatic settings in toneScan Studio, with no manual corrections.</p><p>Shot on a Fujifilm X-T5 with toneLight RGB.</p>",
      "info": "Sits in the dark column on desktop and under the button on phones."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Button"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_scans_cta",
      "label": "Show the button",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Hidden automatically on the lite template, where the gallery it points at is not on the page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_text",
      "label": "Button text",
      "default": "See sample scans"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "Button link",
      "default": "#gallery",
      "info": "A URL, or an #anchor on this page such as #gallery."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Film edge printing"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "edge_stock",
      "label": "Stock designation",
      "default": "TONE PT 200/24°",
      "info": "Printed along the top edge of every frame, the way a film stock and format are marked on real 35mm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "edge_batch",
      "label": "Batch code",
      "default": "0-2137",
      "info": "Repeats along the top edge. Kept identical across the whole strip, since one roll is one batch."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "toneScan conversion strip"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
